OL,3,ATV stars to marry in chapel home after
OL,4,Aproposal 'on Welsh soil'
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Great Pottery Throw Down judge
OL,7,FKeith Brymer Jones has told how he and
OL,8,Fhis partner are to marry in their north
OL,9,FWales chapel home after he proposed to
OL,10,Fher "on Welsh soil".
OL,12,FJones said he and actor Marj Hogarth,
OL,13,Fwho are renovating a Grade II-listed
OL,14,Fchapel in Pwllheli, were on tour "and I
OL,15,Fjust thought I ought to really propose
OL,16,Fto her on Welsh soil".
OL,18,FHe proposed during their show at the
OL,19,FNew Theatre in Cardiff, and "the idea
OL,20,Fis to get married in the main hall some
OL,21,Ftime in May of next year".
OL,23,APub: 24-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
